- op: discuss  # 47ee
  at: '2026-05-06T23:24:25Z'  # 47ee
  by: agent  # 47ee
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 47ee
  clock: 4  # 47ee
  nonce: 47ee  # 47ee
  message: "Empirical addendum to ext A scope: WI-fukol survey (2026-05-06) discovered a third producer-leak shape that ext A doesn't catch — DICT-INDEX assignment.\n\nlinkers/pyffi.py:142,157 emits evidence_type values via:\n\n    lib_vars[var_name] = 'ctypes_stdlib_call'  # line 142\n    lib_vars[var_name] = 'cffi_stdlib_call'    # line 157\n\nThen later: evidence_type = lib_vars[var_name]; Edge.create(... evidence_type=evidence_type, ...).\n\next A's _resolve_function_local walks back assignments where target is an ast.Name (kind = 'literal'). It does not handle ast.Subscript targets (lib_vars[var_name] = '...'). The conservative posture (dict-derived RHS = unresolvable, silent skip) means ext A correctly skips this without false-positive — but the leak is real: ctypes_stdlib_call / cffi_stdlib_call are emitted today and were never registered in evidence_types.py until this finding (will register in next PR).\n\nThis adds a fourth blind-spot category to the catalog:\n  1. Literal-kwarg form (caught by original linter)\n  2. Assignment-form to Name (caught by ext A)\n  3. F-string form (advisory only; ext B target)\n  4. Dict-subscript-target assignment-form (NEW; ext C target — the structural-backstop ban-the-variable-form rule covers this)\n\nReinforces the ext B/C value proposition: ext C in particular (banning Symbol(kind=variable, ...) / Edge.create(...=variable, ...) producer shapes) eliminates ALL three remaining blind spots structurally rather than playing whack-a-mole."  # 47ee
